- "Endurance trapped by ice", 1915, Paget colour plate ON 26/16 — State Library of New South Wales (Flickr Commons, "No known copyright
  restrictions") — https://www.flickr.com/photos/statelibraryofnsw/54014794374/
- "The End" (the wreck), Nov 1915 — Library of Congress, LC-DIG-ds-18589 — https://www.loc.gov/item/2013646126/
- Launching the James Caird, 24 Apr 1916 — Library of Congress, LC-USZ62-9523 — https://www.loc.gov/item/2013646116/
- The men waving on Elephant Island, 1916 (date disputed, see SOURCES.md) — Hurley's glass lantern slide, State Library of New South Wales,
  Slides 22/48, via Wikimedia Commons (File:AllSafeAllWell.jpg); the same photograph as Library of Congress LC-USZ62-10323 (Underwood, 1916)
- On the desk: Ocean Camp (LC-USZ62-15943) and "Terrors of the Weddell Sea" (LC-USZ62-16497) — Library of Congress

